This directory contains the presentation material for the lesson.

## Slide decks

### `01_ngra_intro_skeleton.pptx`

Editable skeleton for the first 60 minutes of the lesson. It follows the
lesson-plan sequence from the regulatory context and traditional risk
assessment to NGRA, NAMs, AOPs, kinetics, points of departure, uncertainty,
and evidence integration. The final slides introduce the genotoxicity case
study and transition directly into Lab 1.

The slides contain timing markers, concise source references, and teaching
prompts in the speaker notes. The visual design and examples are intentionally
kept at skeleton level until the content and ordering have been reviewed.

### `theory_panoraima_le_toxicology.pptx`

The uploaded theory deck. It contains the predictive-toxicology, QSAR,
machine-learning, neural-network, model-evaluation, and data-splitting theory
that supports the notebooks. It is currently broader than the two-hour lesson
and should be reduced or moved partly to an appendix when the decks are
combined.
